## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests dynamic programming on partitioning with a non-linear cost function (distinct character count). It's concrete, implementable, and scales well to typical interview constraints.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and partition count
- Precomputing distinct character counts for all substrings (O(n²) with two pointers)
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartitionDistinct(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dist = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(0));

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    const seen = new Set();
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      seen.add(s[j]);
      dist[i][j] = seen.size;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(i, k); t++) {
      for (let j = t - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j][t - 1] + dist[j][i - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const partitions = [];
  let [i, t] = [n, k];
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = prev[i][t];
    partitions.unshift([j, i - 1]);
    i = j;
    t--;
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], partitions };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a DP over partitions where block value depends on both max and sum, plus reconstruction of segments. Encourages discussion on precomputation of range maxima and efficient transitions.

## Key Concepts

- DP over partitioning with fixed number of segments
- Block value using max and sum requires precomputation
- Path reconstruction for exact endpoints

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxBlockPartition(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  const pref=new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1]=pref[i]+A[i];
  // precompute max for all subarrays
  const maxSub=Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){ let m=A[i]; for(let j=i;j<n;j++){ m=Math.max(m,A[j]); maxSub[i][j]=m; } }
  const blockVal=(l,r)=> (r-l+1)*maxSub[l][r] - (pref[r+1]-pref[l]);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t];
      par[i][t]=[i-1,t];
      for(let s=1;s<=i;s++){
        const val=dp[s-1][t-1] + blockVal(s-1,i-1);
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; par[i][t]=[s-1,t-1]; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would backtrack from (n,k) using par
  return {best: dp[n][k], par};
}
```

